"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JF8BBG921S010M4\",\"title\":\"Carboneers & Terrafront High Tech Biochar — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Carboneers & Terrafront High Tech Biochar\",\"Carboneers\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"NYW2\",\"PROTOCOL DETAILS\",\"Current protocol version\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"NYW2\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.0\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"27 Mar 2025\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"25 Feb 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://Carboneers.earth\",\"t\":\"Carboneers\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.0\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V/prj_1JF8BBG921S010M4/pjd_1JXMETX041S0V43Q/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JEXX4F1D1S0TN3V/prj_1JF8BBG921S010M4/pjd_1JMYDV7311S05KDB/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nCarboneers & Terrafront High Tech Biochar\\nCarboneers\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\nNYW2\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.0\\nAccreditation\\nSummary\\n\\nCarboneers and Terrafront partner with smallholder farmers in Assam, India, to produce biochar from paddy straw waste streams with a small amount coming from corn stover. Using a centralized, high-tech pyrolysis facility tweaked to maximize biochar yield and quality, the process ensures emissions control, efficiency, quality, and operator safety. Once produced, the biochar is mixed with compost or manure and applied to nearby fields.\\n\\nAssam, India\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 26 Mar 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nSite visit\\n\\nIsometric’s qualified VVB conducts a site visit, comparing the project facility against the documentation provided. The required cadence for site visits is defined in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n27 Mar 2025\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n25 Feb 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"